From ff2d34cbdcf00133415a7baf84bfae8917b34f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 15:57:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0112 -- native Gravis Ultrasound (GF1) audio
 backend

Campaign 3 Phase 0. A native GF1 wavetable audio backend (new
src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_gus.c) driven OUT-OF-BAND, exactly like the
shipped AdLib/OPL path (SDL/0110's PIT/OPL exports). It is NOT an SDL
streaming audio device: there is no audio bootstrap, no SDL audio device
opened, no SDL3_mixer PCM sink, and no SDL_INIT_AUDIO involvement. The engine
brings the card up via SDL_DOSGusInit() (mirroring how the AdLib path uses
SDL_DOSOpl2Detect + the pump start), then uploads sample bytes into the
card's on-board DRAM and commands GF1 hardware voices through the exports in
SDL3/SDL_dosgus.h. The GF1 mixes up to N voices in hardware straight to its
DAC; the host CPU does allocation + event dispatch only.

Why DOS needs this: a GUS-only machine (no Sound Blaster) cannot open
SDL_INIT_AUDIO at all today, so it had to boot AUDIO_OFF. The engine adds a
`gus` boot-mode that omits SDL_INIT_AUDIO (like `adlib`) and drives the GF1
purely through these exports -- enabling native wavetable audio on a GUS box
and moving the whole PCM mix off the P54C (the 50fps KPI angle). The Sound
Blaster path is wholly untouched (this patch adds no audio bootstrap and edits
no shared audio core file), so it stays byte-identical.

Phase 0 scope (out-of-band model, per the GUS-NATIVE-DESIGN model-B amendment):
- SDL_DOSGusInit/Shutdown: parse ULTRASND/ULTRADIR/VOICES hints via SDL_GetHint
  (never getenv; the engine bridges the real env vars), GF1 reset, DRAM
  peek/poke detect (0x43/0x44/3X7) + 256K-boundary sizing, set active voices
  (reg 0x0E -> rate), DAC enable, hook+lock the GF1 IRQ; Shutdown tears down.
  SKIP_DETECTION escape hatch for DOSBox/PicoGUS bring-up.
- DRAM upload (verbatim, no sign munging): programmed-I/O poke (small,
  always-correct, default) + one-shot 8237 DMA bulk into a DOS_AllocateDMAMemory
  bounce buffer (freed after; not a ring); 16-bit samples bank-aligned.
- Voice ops alloc/start/stop/freq/vol/pan via per-voice regs. Driver owns all
  GF1 conversions (FC = hz*1024/rate; 8-bit addr split hi=addr>>7
  lo=(addr&0x7F)<<9; 16-bit bank-interleave quirk; linear->4.8-log volume;
  0-255->4-bit pan). Voices pinned at 28 (-> ~22050 Hz) set once at Init.
- Engine owns voice lifecycle: the driver never auto-returns a wave-ended
  voice. SDL_DOSGusGetState refreshes voice_active_mask from the GF1
  voice-stopped hardware status (double-read for the latch quirk); the engine
  polls it and calls StopVoice to reap. The light GF1 ISR only ACKs pending
  voice IRQs + flags DMA-terminal; it never touches the alloc pool. Locked
  code + globals.
- SDL_DOSGusResetDram(keep_bytes) rewinds the DRAM bump cursor while preserving
  a low keep region (a persistent SFX bank survives per-song .pat swaps).
- New hints SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_GUS_{ULTRASND,ULTRADIR,VOICES,SKIP_DETECTION,
  DIAG} (diag default-OFF).
- REQUIRED detect banner "audio: SDL/0112 GUS GF1 detect: present=..." for the
  smoke BANNERS array.

GF1 register indices cross-checked against the DOSBox-X gus.cpp emulation (the
campaign's functional witness) + the GUS SDK programming model; the IRQ/DMA
latch + a few conversions are ACCURATE-BUT-CONFIRM inline, pending the
operator's g2k register-accuracy pass (dosbox_not_proxy: DOSBox is a functional
witness only). Validated here by a clean libSDL3.a link with all 11 exports
present and no audio bootstrap symbol.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
